# .host-software — the Where room recipe (STRUCTURE.md). One stanza per
# component: source URL, the pinned canonical SHA, the canonical branch, any
# parallel-line worktrees, and the reproducibility record.
#
# The crate migrated 2026-09-13 (component cb7bfb4) from the former
# rope-agentic monorepo (tools/ds-lite-punch/), unmodified; the musl
# release build reproduces the deployed artifact byte-identically, so the
# waiver (call/0012) is retired by call/0016.
[software "ds-lite-punch"]
	url   = https://github.com/slartibardfast/ds-lite-punch.git
	pin   = 43df0b50a6884a7b4969360fc5ca242b048a3e51
	branch = main
	toolchain = ghcr.io/rust-cross/rust-musl-cross@sha256:ce75e9174325d4fbb3de85c309e2d7ca29f7500169bc4b5d2c611ff7e86d549a
	build = cargo build --release --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl
	artifact = target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/ds-lite-punch 777d518981ee43a5d2f15c0f08043a3d069bd29b69afa51dc66c419263817a60
# The toolchain is a digest-pinned container rather than a target triple:
# `--verify-build` runs the recorded `build` inside it, so the image is what
# reproduces the artifact and a movable tag would invalidate every hash
# recorded under it. The hash above was re-derived inside that image by the
# component's own CI, twice, with the two runs agreeing byte for byte, and the
# lane publishes the binary it built, so a deployment takes those bytes rather
# than a local build's (call/0032).
#
# This development host has no container runtime, so its own target/ builds
# with the ambient compiler and hashes differently (8e21070e...). That is a
# property of the host, not a defect in the record: a local build is for
# iteration, and the binary on the test router was installed from the lane's
# artifact and checked against the hash above before it was started.
